{"command":"cat > results/research/issue117/runs/run_2f4348aa17bd4256/agents/geometry/candidate.json <<'EOF'
{
  "candidate_id": "geometry-directed-transition-hyperbolic-rq-v1",
  "behavior_problem_id": "directed-next-item-transition-neighborhoods",
  "behavior_evidence_sha256": "793d52dce39a5a8aa3963ff566ae50612114b9d20d31227dfed3d1e9fc653b9b",
  "literature_evidence_sha256": "4cc3a2a41798a1021c2ba891a650c2a5d116f284c040996c5a50aca697cf1653",
  "next_item_hypothesis": "A demonstrated asymmetry is the train-only directed pair 22372→9218 (32 occurrences) versus 9218→22372 (21 occurrences); more broadly, 314605/339519 observed transitions have no observed reverse event. This is not itself proof that an existing recommender fails. The one failure hypothesis is that a content-only, fixed three-token SID can assign items with different directed successor neighborhoods to indistinguishable two-token prefixes, thereby losing the directional neighborhood signal needed to distinguish their next-item targets. Stage2 should reduce this representational collision; Stage3 alone tests whether that helps next-item ranking. The behavior counts are evidence for the trigger, not evidence of a measured SID failure or causal gain.",
  "math_definition": {
    "architecture_and_assignment": "For item i, content encoder fθ maps its content embedding e_i to h_i∈R^32. The shared bounded representation map is P_R(v)=v·min(1,R/||v||₂), with P_R(0)=0 and R=0.9. Set residual r_{i,0}=P_R(h_i). For levels l=1,2,3, let codebook C_l={c_{l,k}∈R^32:k∈{0,…,255}}. Compute u_{i,l}=P_R(r_{i,l−1}); assign a_{i,l}=argmin_k D_c²(u_{i,l},P_R(c_{l,k})), ties by lowest k; set q_{i,l}=P_R(c_{l,a_{i,l}}); then update residual in this exact order: map u_{i,l}=P_R(r_{i,l−1}), project codewords q_{i,l}=P_R(c_{l,a_{i,l}}), assign using the scored distance, subtract r_{i,l}=P_R(u_{i,l}−q_{i,l}). The global item SID is exactly (a_{i,1},a_{i,2},a_{i,3}), with no user or context input. Every vector entering a distance is projected by P_R first; residual updates are projected before any subsequent scoring.",
    "curvature_and_stability": "Use a single scalar parameter c∈[0,0.1], with hyperbolic arm c=0.1 and flat control c=0 as the continuous limit of the same implementation. For x,y∈R^32 already projected into ||·||₂≤R, define A=||x−y||₂², B=(1−c||x||₂²)(1−c||y||₂²), z=1+2cA/B, w=z−1, and the stable arcosh(z)=log1p(w+sqrt(w(w+2))). The single scored squared distance is D_c²(x,y)=d_c(x,y)²=(1/c)·[log1p(w+sqrt(w(w+2)))]² for c>0. Its exact c→0 limit is D_0²(x,y)=4||x−y||₂²; the unsquared distance tends to 2||x−y||₂. All objectives use the squared power D² in both arms. Domain policy: reject non-finite inputs; project all distance arguments to ||x||≤R; require c∈[0,0.1], so B>0 and z≥1; clamp only roundoff in w to max(w,0) before sqrt, and do not clamp distances or logits otherwise. For the c-dependent exponential map use exp^c_0(v)=tanh(sqrt(c)||v||₂)·v/(sqrt(c)||v||₂), with value 0 at v=0; its c→0 limit is the identity v. If used to map a vector into the ball, apply P_R immediately after the map before scoring. The c-dependent open-ball radius (1−epsilon)/sqrt(c), with epsilon=0.001, has no defined c=0 value; the flat arm does not use that radius or a ball projection and instead uses the shared P_R with R=0.9. Thus both arms have the same fixed bounded feasible region and representation map.",
    "train_transition_target": "Let V be the fixed set of train-split item IDs, M=|V|, and n_{ij} the count of consecutive directed transitions i→j computed only from train split. For source i with m_i=Σ_{j∈V}n_{ij}>0 define the frozen empirical target p_{ij}=n_{ij}/m_i for j∈V; sources with m_i=0 are excluded. This target is computed from labels and counts before training, contains no model parameter, and is not recomputed from predictions. For item vectors z_i=P_R(h_i), transition loss is L_trans=−(1/|S|)Σ_{i∈S}Σ_{j∈V}p_{ij} log softmax_{j∈V}(−D_c²(z_i,z_j)/τ), where S={i∈V:m_i>0}, τ=0.07, softmax is normalized over the full fixed train-item set V, and the reduction is the mean over eligible sources and sum over each source's target distribution. If S is empty, L_trans=0 and the transition term is disabled for that run. This is train-transition supervision only; no validation/test event or batch-derived target is used.",
    "quantization_objective": "For training item minibatch I, define stop-gradient assignments a_{i,l} by the assignment rule above, q_{i,l}=P_R(c_{l,a_{i,l}}), and u_{i,l}=P_R(r_{i,l−1}). Define L_rec=(1/(|I|·3))Σ_{i∈I}Σ_{l=1}^3 D_c²(u_{i,l},q_{i,l}); define L_commit=(1/(|I|·3))Σ_{i∈I}Σ_{l=1}^3 D_c²(u_{i,l},sg(q_{i,l})); total L=L_rec+0.25L_commit+0.1L_trans. Each level/item term is averaged uniformly; no code-frequency reweighting. Empty I is an invalid training batch, not assigned a zero loss. The empirical p target is label-derived and frozen, while assignments are stop-gradient for discrete code selection, which breaks target/parameter circularity. Existing Stage2 epochs, batch size, schedule, seeds, optimizer, and codebook initialization remain exactly as configured; no new training protocol is introduced."
  },
  "hyperbolic_necessity": "The hypothesized failure is specifically about representing a branching, asymmetric successor neighborhood under a fixed-length SID, not merely fitting semantic content. Negative curvature is a motivated, falsifiable inductive bias because it can allocate representational separation across nested/unevenly populated neighborhoods while preserving a common bounded representation domain. Train-only directed transitions provide the permitted behavioral signal. The observed asymmetry and cited HypRQ-VAE/VarLenRec intersection motivate this test but establish neither that the item space is truly hyperbolic nor that hyperbolic encoding improves ranking. A matched flat limit is therefore essential.",
  "euclidean_control": "The flat arm is exactly the same code path and objective with c=0, replacing D_c² by its exact limit 4||x−y||². It has the same encoder, three codebooks, dimensions, parameter count, shared P_R map and R, assignments, train-only transition target, initialization, optimizer, schedule, seeds, epochs, batches, and compute budget. It is not an unbounded or differently parameterized Euclidean model. No graph arm is included.",
  "effect_site": "Code assignment and codebook geometry, with the same squared-distance reconstruction, commitment, and train-transition objective in both arms. Expected Stage2 movement: validation Hard-L1 ER decreases; distinct two-token prefixes increase; L3 collision decreases; refinement gain increases; conditional G3 increases. These are diagnostics, not training targets or Stage3 ranking metrics. Stage3 is the existing downstream T5 next-item ranker and is not part of this candidate mechanism.",
  "real_trigger_measurement": "The observed directed-pair table gives one concrete asymmetry: 22372→9218 occurs 32 times and its reverse occurs 21 times; 314605 of 339519 observed transitions have no observed reverse. Mean next-item entropy is 4.844072338042215 bits. These train-only aggregate measurements identify directional next-item structure worth testing, but do not establish that this model currently fails on those transitions. Do not inspect or use validation/test behavior to choose items, targets, parameters, or the mechanism.",
  "training_only_inputs": "Item content embeddings and consecutive item transitions from train split only. No validation/test behavior, future events, prediction-time user context, or batch composition enters targets, assignments, or loss definitions. Train-split transitions are permitted supervision under CLAUDE.md rule 16.",
  "stable_global_sid": true,
  "protocol": {
    "latent_dim": 32,
    "levels": 3,
    "codes_per_level": 256,
    "hyperparameter_sweep": false,
    "uses_future_events": false
  },
  "falsifier": {
    "stage2_diagnostics": [
      {"name": "validation_Hard-L1_ER", "direction": "decrease_vs_flat", "minimum_effect": 0.01, "seed_rule": "paired identical frozen seeds; effect is flat minus hyperbolic relative ER, then arithmetic mean across registered seeds"},
      {"name": "distinct_two-token_prefixes", "direction": "increase_vs_flat", "minimum_effect": 0.01, "seed_rule": "paired identical frozen seeds; effect is hyperbolic minus flat fraction of distinct prefixes, then arithmetic mean across registered seeds"},
      {"name": "L3_collision", "direction": "decrease_vs_flat", "minimum_effect": 0.01, "seed_rule": "paired identical frozen seeds; effect is flat minus hyperbolic collision rate, then arithmetic mean across registered seeds"},
      {"name": "refinement_gain", "direction": "increase_vs_flat", "minimum_effect": 0.01, "seed_rule": "paired identical frozen seeds; effect is hyperbolic minus flat refinement gain, then arithmetic mean across registered seeds"},
      {"name": "conditional_G3", "direction": "increase_vs_flat", "minimum_effect": 0.01, "seed_rule": "paired identical frozen seeds; effect is hyperbolic minus flat conditional G3, then arithmetic mean across registered seeds"}
    ],
    "stage3_behavioral_test": {
      "metric": "test_R@10",
      "direction": "increase_vs_flat",
      "minimum_effect": 0.005,
      "seed_rule": "paired identical frozen seeds and identical existing Stage3 protocol; effect is hyperbolic minus flat test_R@10, then arithmetic mean across registered seeds"
    },
    "classification": {
      "falsified_if": "any registered non-NULL stage2_diagnostic effect is below its own minimum_effect OR the non-NULL stage3_behavioral_test effect is below its own minimum_effect",
      "passed_if": "every registered stage2_diagnostic effect and stage3_behavioral_test effect is non-NULL and is at least its own minimum_effect",
      "mixed_if": "at least one registered effect is at least its own minimum_effect AND at least one registered effect is below its own minimum_effect, with no NULL effect",
      "null_outcome": "If any seed-wise or aggregated change is undefined or non-finite because of a zero denominator, missing evaluation, or empty stratum, that effect is NULL; comparison with any NULL seed is inconclusive and the run is neither passed nor falsified."
    }
  }
}
